# dataset=GoogleLocal  d_emb=64 k_train=5 lr=1e-3 seed=5 patience 5 cap 100
# experiment=duv_cand_pop cell=d64_k5 tag=run_1  (chained; see DRIVER.log)
# branch=feature/duv-with-cand-pop commit=0578e9e4
# head: score = mix([-d_H, log1p(cand_popularity)]), Linear(2,1,bias=False), w init [1,0].
#       163 head params. LOSS: softmax CE, unchanged from master.
#
# WHAT IT IS. The master baseline plus ONE extra scalar feature: how many edges the
#   candidate had strictly before the query cutoff. w init [1,0] means the score STARTS
#   as exactly the baseline -d_H (geo_temp pinned at 1) with the popularity channel
#   contributing nothing, so w[1] has to earn its weight rather than being granted it.
#
# log1p NOT log. get_candidate_popularity returns 0 for a node with no prior edge and
#   cold candidates are common; log(0) = -inf would NaN the first batch. log1p maps
#   0 -> 0, which is also the right inert value for a cold node.
#
# THE RISK, STATED UP FRONT. w[1] is inert at init in VALUE but not in GRADIENT:
#   measured d(CE)/dw = [1.97e-04, 7.65e-01] at init, so the popularity weight carries
#   ~3900x the gradient of the distance weight and will move immediately. That is NOT
#   the earned-range profile of d0_u*d0_v, whose gradient was genuinely ~0 (2.3e-07).
#   Every head on this suite that CAPTURED the score in the first epoch or two finished
#   badly -- d0v captured at ep1 with w[0] -> -30.6 and scored 0.4567 against the
#   baseline 0.5626. WATCH w[1] AT EPOCH 1. If it jumps and w[0] collapses, this is
#   that failure mode and the run can be called early.
#
# PRIOR ON POPULARITY. TGB-Seq test negatives are UNIFORM over the destination pool,
#   popularity-blind: measured corr(log10 train-popularity, log10 test-negative-freq)
#   = +0.0137 on ML-20M, rare pool nodes averaging 1340.2 appearances against popular
#   ones at 1340.6. A popularity channel therefore cannot help by exploiting the
#   negative sampler -- it can only help if popularity genuinely predicts the POSITIVE.
#   A per-node popularity bias table was also part of the withdrawn historical-best
#   configs that CLAUDE.md records as unstable. Treat a large early gain with suspicion.
#
# SEED-5 BASELINE (commit 07dcc1e6), the number this must beat, val / test / stop-ep:
#   GoogleLocal 0.6818 / 0.6535 / 44     YouTube  0.6467 / 0.5626 / 19
#   Flickr      0.6581 / 0.6251 / 13     Patent   0.1262 / 0.2263 / 13
#   ML-20M      0.2826 / 0.2429 / 7      Taobao   0.5536 / 0.5313 / 4
#   Yelp        0.6633 / 0.6204 / 14     WikiLink 0.6682 / 0.6592 / 15
#
# WATCH: (a) w[1] at ep1-2, see THE RISK above;  (b) w[0] -- if it collapses toward 0
#   the geometry has been abandoned for the popularity shortcut;  (c) PATENT especially
#   -- its walks are structurally dead at length 2 (mean 2.20, only 0.3% reach 5), so
#   the bag is the seed plus one neighbour and a cheap non-geometric feature has the
#   most room to take over there;  (d) VAL/TEST DRIFT -- on Patent val is a POOR
#   selector (baseline best val 0.1262 -> test 0.2263, while a recent arm reached a
#   HIGHER val 0.1276 at a LOWER test 0.2023). Record peak test AND test@val-ckpt.
#
